 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Tuned for a 5 V gate. Threshold sits between 0.9 and 1.8 V at 250 µA. Maximum on-resistance at 4 A is 42 mΩ with 3 V of drive, 32 mΩ with 4.5 V and 30 mΩ with 8 V. Charging the gate to 4.5 V takes 2.1 nC typical (2.7 nC max); gate-drain charge is 0.4 nC typical. The gate may go 10 V positive and 8 V negative of the source; internal gate resistance is 1.3 Ω typical, 2.6 Ω max."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Current ratings",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Three continuous ratings apply: 5 A set by the package, 19 A for the die with the case held at 25 °C, and 7.3 A with the part on 1 in² of 2 oz copper (53 °C/W typical to ambient). Figure 12 holds the package limit of 5 A flat up to about 140 °C case temperature. Pulsed current reaches 57 A for pulses of 100 µs or less at 1 % duty."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Heat and mounting",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Junction-to-case resistance is at most 7.4 °C/W. Junction-to-ambient depends on the copper under the part: at most 67 °C/W on 1 in² of 2 oz copper, rising to 228 °C/W on a minimum-size pad. Power dissipation is 2.4 W on the 1 in² pad and 17 W with the case at 25 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature behaviour",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "On-resistance climbs with temperature: Figure 8 puts it near 1.43 times the 25 °C value at 125 °C with 4.5 V drive, and Figure 7 shows 26 mΩ at 25 °C against about 37 mΩ at 125 °C with 4.5 V on the gate. Threshold falls from about 1.5 V at –55 °C to about 0.9 V at 150 °C (Figure 6)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode and avalanche",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "The body diode drops 0.85 V typical, 1 V max, at 4 A. Recovering from 4 A at 300 A/µs with 13.5 V applied it stores 6.4 nC and takes 12.9 ns. A single avalanche pulse of 19 A through 0.1 mH, gate resistance 25 Ω, is rated at 18 mJ; Figure 11 gives the allowed peak avalanche current against time in avalanche at case temperatures of 25 °C and 125 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Layout",
   "page": 9,
   "text": "TI application note SLPA005 covers PCB layout for reduced switching ringing."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Handling",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "ESD protection on the part is limited. Keep the leads shorted together, or store the parts in conductive foam, so static cannot damage the gate."
  }
 ],
